  "Question": "Which of the following transformations, read from left to right, is a factorization?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x(x+1)=x^2+x\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2-4=(x+2)(x-2)\\)",
    "C": "\\(x^2+2x+1=x(x+2)+1\\)",
    "D": "\\((x+1)(x-1)=x^2-1\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The result of factorization must be a product of polynomial expressions. A and D are polynomial multiplication; the right-hand side of C still contains a plus sign and is not in product form.",
